When should values from different sources become one result? Four operators answer that question
in four different ways:

- {% highlight %}combineLatest{% /highlight %}: any input changes.
- {% highlight %}withLatestFrom{% /highlight %}: one source leads.
- {% highlight %}zip{% /highlight %}: pair by position.
- {% highlight %}forkJoin{% /highlight %}: wait for the final values.

Same inputs, same timeline. Only the combination rule changes.

## The experiment

Two inputs, one shared clock. All examples subscribe at 0s. Each input emits two values and then
completes. There are no errors.

| Input | Emits | Completes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A | A1 at 1s, A2 at 4s | 6s |
| B | B1 at 2s, B2 at 5s | 7s |

{% diagram id="rxjs-combining-streams/experiment" alt="Timeline of the two inputs: A emits A1 at 1s and A2 at 4s and completes at 6s; B emits B1 at 2s and B2 at 5s and completes at 7s." caption="Time runs left to right; a vertical bar marks completion." /%}

In the outputs, `[A2,B1]` means one emitted pair. The lines show events over time, not separate
threads, and every diagram uses the same scale.

## {% highlight %}combineLatest{% /highlight %}: any input can trigger

Wait for both inputs to emit once. Then emit their latest values whenever either one changes.

```ts
combineLatest([a$, b$]);
```

{% diagram id="rxjs-combining-streams/combinelatest" alt="Timeline for combineLatest: the output emits [A1,B1] at 2s, [A2,B1] at 4s and [A2,B2] at 5s, and completes at 7s." caption="Values are pairs: each dot on Out is one emission." /%}

First result at 2s; further results at 4s and 5s. No initial value from one input? No combined
value yet. Here, the output completes at 7s, after both inputs. Use it for a view model built from
several changing inputs.

## {% highlight %}withLatestFrom{% /highlight %}: one source leads

Only A can trigger. B updates the stored value; it never triggers an output on its own. A is the
source here.

```ts
a$.pipe(withLatestFrom(b$));
```

{% diagram id="rxjs-combining-streams/withlatestfrom" alt="Timeline for withLatestFrom: A1 at 1s produces nothing because B has not emitted yet; A2 at 4s emits [A2,B1]; B2 at 5s produces no output; the output completes with A at 6s." caption="Only A's emissions can produce an output." /%}

A1 is skipped: B has not emitted yet. It is not queued. At 4s, A2 uses B1. B2 at 5s produces no
output. Here, the output completes with A at 6s. Use it for a submit event that reads the latest
form state.

## {% highlight %}zip{% /highlight %}: first with first

Wait until every input has a value for the next pair. Consume each value once, in input order.

```ts
zip(a$, b$);
```

{% diagram id="rxjs-combining-streams/zip" alt="Timeline for zip: the output emits [A1,B1] at 2s and [A2,B2] at 5s; A2 waits from 4s to 5s for B2." caption="Each value is used in exactly one pair." /%}

A2 waits from 4s to 5s for B2. It does not reuse B1. At 6s, A is complete and its queue is empty:
done. A much faster input can build up a large queue. Use it for two sequences that must be paired
by index.

## {% highlight %}forkJoin{% /highlight %}: one final snapshot

Wait for every input to emit and complete. Then emit their last values once and complete.

```ts
forkJoin([a$, b$]);
```

{% diagram id="rxjs-combining-streams/forkjoin" alt="Timeline for forkJoin: a single output, [A2,B2], at 7s when B completes, and then the output completes." caption="One emission, only after every input has completed." /%}

A finishing at 6s is not enough: B finishes at 7s. An input that never completes can keep you
waiting. In RxJS 7, an empty input completes the join with no value. Use it for several finite HTTP
requests needed together.

## Choose the trigger

Ask when to emit, then choose the tool. The same values can lead to very different outputs.

| When should it emit? | Operator | Outputs |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Any input changes | `combineLatest` | 2s, 4s, 5s |
| Only the source emits | `withLatestFrom` | 4s |
| The next pair is ready | `zip` | 2s, 5s |
| All inputs complete | `forkJoin` | 7s |

These tools combine streams; they do not create threads. An unhandled error in any input fails the
combined output.

{% quiz %}
{% question text="Saving must use the latest form state, but a change in the form alone must not save anything. Which operator replaces `???`?" options=["`combineLatest`", "`withLatestFrom`", "`zip`", "`forkJoin`"] answer=2 explanation="With `withLatestFrom`, only the source (`submit$`) triggers an output; `form$` just updates the stored value." %}
```ts
submit$.pipe(???(form$)).subscribe(([, form]) => save(form));
```
{% /question %}

{% question text="A dashboard's view model must update whenever the filters or the data change. Which operator?" options=["`combineLatest`", "`withLatestFrom`", "`zip`", "`forkJoin`"] answer=1 explanation="`combineLatest` emits the latest values of all inputs whenever any of them changes, once each has emitted at least once." /%}

{% question text="A page needs three finite HTTP requests, all of them, before it renders. Which operator?" options=["`combineLatest`", "`withLatestFrom`", "`zip`", "`forkJoin`"] answer=4 explanation="`forkJoin` waits for every input to emit and complete, then emits their last values once: one final snapshot." /%}

{% question text="In the experiment (A1 at 1s, B1 at 2s), why is there no output at 1s?" options=["A1 is queued until B emits", "B has not emitted yet, so A1 is skipped", "`withLatestFrom` waits for A to complete"] answer=2 explanation="When A1 arrives, B has no value to read, so A1 produces nothing. It is not queued: the first output is A2 with B1, at 4s." %}
```ts
a$.pipe(withLatestFrom(b$));
```
{% /question %}

{% question text="You pass `forkJoin` an input that never completes, like a form's `valueChanges`. What happens?" options=["It emits each time the form changes", "It never emits: it keeps waiting for that input to complete", "It emits once, with the form's first value"] answer=2 explanation="`forkJoin` emits only after every input completes. An input that never completes keeps it waiting." /%}
{% /quiz %}

Sources: the RxJS 7 API for [combineLatest](https://rxjs.dev/api/index/function/combineLatest), [withLatestFrom](https://rxjs.dev/api/operators/withLatestFrom), [zip](https://rxjs.dev/api/index/function/zip) and [forkJoin](https://rxjs.dev/api/index/function/forkJoin).
